These regulations reinforce corporate climate accountability, improve investor confidence, and align the UK with global ESG disclosure standards.', 'These regulations, which came into force on April 6, 2022, amend the Companies Act 2006 to introduce mandatory climate-related financial disclosures for large UK companies. The legislation aligns with the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (TCFD) recommendations, ensuring businesses assess and disclose their exposure to climate risks.

