Executive Remuneration & Incentives:
Executive pay must align with company performance and long-term sustainability goals.
Clawback provisions must be included in remuneration policies to recover bonuses if misconduct or poor performance occurs.
‘Comply or Explain’ Approach:
Companies must either comply with the Code’s provisions or provide clear explanations for non-compliance in their annual reports.
The 2024 revision strengthens internal control accountability (Provision 29) but allows companies until January 1, 2026, to comply with new reporting requirements.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_7', ARRAY['sdg13', 'uk', 'sdg7', 'sdg11', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg9']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('19ca406d-fa17-500a-8ff5-e460c7c3bbf5', 'UK Principles for Purposeful Business. How to deliver the', 'Principles for Purposeful Business. How to deliver the framework for the Future of the Corporation, 2018', 'The Future of the Corporation programme is one of the largest and most ambitious ever conducted by the British Academy, the UK’s national academy for the humanities and social sciences. It lies at the heart of the future of capitalism, the future of humanity and the future of our planet. This second report builds on the November 2018 report, “Reforming business for the 21st century”. It revisits the case for change and highlights that climate change, the urgency of delivering on the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), technological developments, the increasing dominance of companies without significant tangible assets, and negative perceptions of business make this agenda particularly urgent. It identifies how change can and should be achieved. It sets out a series of principles to guide lawmakers and business leaders in any jurisdiction towards the policies and practices that can release the potential of business to profitably solve the problems of people and planet, and to prevent business from profiting from harm. The findings are summarised below.', 'The Future of the Corporation programme is one of the largest and most ambitious ever conducted by the British Academy, the UK’s national academy for the humanities and social sciences. It lies at the heart of the future of capitalism, the future of humanity and the future of our planet. This second report builds on the November 2018 report, “Reforming business for the 21st century”. It revisits the case for change and highlights that climate change, the urgency of delivering on the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), technological developments, the increasing dominance of companies without significant tangible assets, and negative perceptions of business make this agenda particularly urgent. It identifies how change can and should be achieved. It sets out a series of principles to guide lawmakers and business leaders in any jurisdiction towards the policies and practices that can release the potential of business to profitably solve the problems of people and planet, and to prevent business from profiting from harm. The findings are summarised below.', 'The Future of the Corporation programme is one of the largest and most ambitious ever conducted by the British Academy, the UK’s national academy for the humanities and social sciences. It lies at the heart of the future of capitalism, the future of humanity and the future of our planet. This second report builds on the November 2018 report, “Reforming business for the 21st century”. It revisits the case for change and highlights that climate change, the urgency of delivering on the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), technological developments, the increasing dominance of companies without significant tangible assets, and negative perceptions of business make this agenda particularly urgent. It identifies how change can and should be achieved. It sets out a series of principles to guide lawmakers and business leaders in any jurisdiction towards the policies and practices that can release the potential of business to profitably solve the problems of people and planet, and to prevent business from profiting from harm. The findings are summarised below.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_89', ARRAY['sdg13', 'voluntary_frameworks', 'uk', 'disclosure', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('7eab5930-cb91-542d-bbf5-80e4d7bc858a', 'UK Strategic Report', 'Guidance on the Strategic Report, 2018', 'The FRC believes that encouraging entities1 to prepare a high quality strategic report – which provides shareholders with a holistic and meaningful picture of an entity''s business model, strategy, development, performance, position and future prospects – is a key part of achieving this purpose.', 'The FRC believes that encouraging entities1 to prepare a high quality strategic report – which provides shareholders with a holistic and meaningful picture of an entity''s business model, strategy, development, performance, position and future prospects – is a key part of achieving this purpose.', 'The FRC believes that encouraging entities1 to prepare a high quality strategic report – which provides shareholders with a holistic and meaningful picture of an entity''s business model, strategy, development, performance, position and future prospects – is a key part of achieving this purpose.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_90', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'mandatory', 'uk', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('080d2c7b-023c-50d5-883c-08385bc1a57e', 'UK Board Effectiveness', 'Guidance on Board Effectiveness, 2018', 'In July 2018 the FRC published a fully revised Guidance on Board Effectiveness (PDF) to support the 2018 UK Corporate Governance Code. This replaces the 2011 version (PDF). The Guidance is intended to stimulate thinking on how boards can carry out their role most  effectively and is designed to help boards with their actions and decisions when reporting on the application of the Code’s Principles.', 'In July 2018 the FRC published a fully revised Guidance on Board Effectiveness (PDF) to support the 2018 UK Corporate Governance Code. This replaces the 2011 version (PDF). The Guidance is intended to stimulate thinking on how boards can carry out their role most  effectively and is designed to help boards with their actions and decisions when reporting on the application of the Code’s Principles.', 'In July 2018 the FRC published a fully revised Guidance on Board Effectiveness (PDF) to support the 2018 UK Corporate Governance Code. This replaces the 2011 version (PDF). The Guidance is intended to stimulate thinking on how boards can carry out their role most  effectively and is designed to help boards with their actions and decisions when reporting on the application of the Code’s Principles.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_91', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'uk', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('1f4c2421-a493-5495-8ac7-be3085f350c2', 'UK Companies (Miscellaneous Reporting) Regulations', 'The Companies (Miscellaneous Reporting) Regulations 2018', 'The Companies (Miscellaneous Reporting) Regulations 2018 in the UK amend reporting requirements for companies, including statements on section 172(1) and directors'' remuneration policy. Targeted at large and medium-sized companies, the policy aims to enhance transparency and accountability in corporate reporting.', 'The Companies (Miscellaneous Reporting) Regulations 2018 in the UK amend reporting requirements for companies, including statements on section 172(1) and directors'' remuneration policy. Targeted at large and medium-sized companies, the policy aims to enhance transparency and accountability in corporate reporting.', 'The Companies (Miscellaneous Reporting) Regulations 2018 in the UK amend reporting requirements for companies, including statements on section 172(1) and directors'' remuneration policy. Targeted at large and medium-sized companies, the policy aims to enhance transparency and accountability in corporate reporting.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2018-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/185_117', ARRAY['sdg16', 'mandatory', 'uk', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('f70228e9-d48b-5162-be98-7fb5aaaf8e98', 'UK Code for Sports Governance', 'A Code for Sports Governance, 2017', 'This code, launched in October 2016, became mandatory for those who seek Government and National Lottery funding from April 2017. In 2020 it was announced that a review of the Code would be undertaken, incorporating sector research and a public consultation. Changes to the Code''s requirements were announced in July 2021 and the full Code and accompanying commentary were published in December 2021. The Code sets out the levels of transparency, accountability and financial integrity that will be required to obtain public funding.', 'This code, launched in October 2016, became mandatory for those who seek Government and National Lottery funding from April 2017. In 2020 it was announced that a review of the Code would be undertaken, incorporating sector research and a public consultation. Changes to the Code''s requirements were announced in July 2021 and the full Code and accompanying commentary were published in December 2021. The Code sets out the levels of transparency, accountability and financial integrity that will be required to obtain public funding.', 'This code, launched in October 2016, became mandatory for those who seek Government and National Lottery funding from April 2017. In 2020 it was announced that a review of the Code would be undertaken, incorporating sector research and a public consultation. Changes to the Code''s requirements were announced in July 2021 and the full Code and accompanying commentary were published in December 2021. The Code sets out the levels of transparency, accountability and financial integrity that will be required to obtain public funding.', 'UK', 'climate', 'in_force', '2017-01-01'::date, 'United Kingdom', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/184_30', ARRAY['sdg14', 'uk', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure', 'sdg15']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
