Group-Level Disclosures:
Parent companies must publish consolidated ESG reports covering all subsidiaries.
Alignment with International Reporting Standards:
Companies can use GRI, UN Global Compact, and other recognized frameworks.
These regulations strengthen corporate sustainability reporting, promote ESG accountability, and align UK law with EU and international disclosure standards.', 'These UK regulations amend the Companies Act 2006 to implement the EU Non-Financial Reporting Directive (2014/95/EU), requiring certain large businesses to disclose non-financial and diversity information. The law enhances corporate transparency and ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) reporting by mandating disclosures on environmental, social, human rights, and anti-corruption matters.

